In the mass basis this gives the following terms of $delta cal(L)^((1))$ (density of $delta S^((1))_"inv" [Hv + phi]$).

_Gauge kinetic terms._ $delta Z_W (-1/2 W^+_(mu nu) W^(- mu nu)) + delta Z_G (-1/4 G^A_(mu nu) G^(A mu nu))$ and, for the neutral pair,
$ - 1/4 [delta Z_(Z Z) Z_(mu nu) Z^(mu nu) + 2 delta Z_(Z gamma) Z_(mu nu) A^(gamma mu nu) + delta Z_(gamma gamma) Ag_(mu nu) A^(gamma mu nu)], $ <eq:bl-dS-kinZA>
$ mat(delim: "(", delta Z_(Z Z), delta Z_(Z gamma); delta Z_(Z gamma), delta Z_(gamma gamma)) = mat(delim: "(", c_W, -s_W; s_W, c_W) mat(delim: "(", delta Z_W, 0; 0, delta Z_B) mat(delim: "(", c_W, s_W; -s_W, c_W) . $ <eq:bl-dZZA>
The bare neutral fields are $(Z, Ag)^T_0 = (bb(1) + 1/2 delta Z) (Z, Ag)^T$ with the matrix $delta Z$ of @eq:bl-dZZA, whose entries are
$ & 16 pi^2 ep thin delta Z_(Z Z) = (33 gw^2 c_W^2 - 43 gy^2 s_W^2)/18, quad 16 pi^2 ep thin delta Z_(gamma gamma) = -5/9 e^2, \
  & 16 pi^2 ep thin delta Z_(Z gamma) = s_W c_W (33 gw^2 + 43 gy^2)/18 . $
The cubic and quartic parts $cal(L)^((r))_3$, $cal(L)^((r))_4$ of $-1/4 F^((r))_(mu nu) F^((r) mu nu)$ ($r = G, W$) carry $c_(r 0) A_0^3 = Z_(c_r) Z_A^(3\/2) c_r A^3$ and $c_(r 0)^2 A_0^4 = Z_(c_r)^2 Z_A^2 c_r^2 A^4$. With $delta Z_(c_r) + 1/2 delta Z^((r))_A = -C^((r))_"ad" lfe$ this gives
$ delta cal(L)^((1)) supset & sum_(r = G, W) [ (delta Z^((r))_A - C^((r))_"ad" lfe) cal(L)^((r))_3 + (delta Z^((r))_A - 2 C^((r))_"ad" lfe) cal(L)^((r))_4 ] \
  = & lfe [2/3 gs^2 cal(L)^((G))_3 - 7/3 gs^2 cal(L)^((G))_4 - 1/6 gw^2 cal(L)^((W))_3 - 13/6 gw^2 cal(L)^((W))_4] . $ <eq:bl-dS-cubic>
In the mass basis $cal(L)^((W))_3$ contains all $W W Ag$ and $W W Z$ vertices of the tree action and $cal(L)^((W))_4$ all $W W W W$, $W W Ag Ag$, $W W Ag Z$ and $W W Z Z$ vertices, with the tree couplings $e$ and $gw c_W$ of @eq:bl-combo. The fermion-loop part of $delta Z^((r))_A$ multiplies the barred form of these terms, as in (b) below.

_Gauge-boson masses._ The bare masses are $M_(W 0) = gw_0 Z_H^(1\/2) v \/ 2$, etc. With $delta M_W^2 = M_W^2 (2 delta Z_gw + delta Z_H)$, $delta M_Z^2 = M_Z^2 (delta Z_H + 2 c_W^2 delta Z_gw + 2 s_W^2 delta Z_gy)$ and $delta M^2_(Z gamma) = M_Z^2 s_W c_W (delta Z_gw - delta Z_gy)$,
#eqbox[$ delta cal(L)^((1)) supset & (M_W^2 delta Z_W + delta M_W^2) W^+ dot W^- + 1/2 (M_Z^2 delta Z_(Z Z) + delta M_Z^2) Z dot Z + (1/2 M_Z^2 delta Z_(Z gamma) + delta M^2_(Z gamma)) Z dot Ag \
  = & lfe [ M_W^2 (2 C_H - Yt - 4 gw^2) W^+ dot W^- + 1/2 M_Z^2 (2 C_H - Yt - 4 gw^2 c_W^2) Z dot Z \
  & #h(3em) - 2 gw^2 s_W c_W M_Z^2 thin Z dot Ag ] . $ <eq:bl-dS-mass>]
Here $2 C_H - Yt = 16 pi^2 ep thin delta Z_H$, and
$ & 16 pi^2 ep thin (delta M_W^2) / M_W^2 = -13/3 gw^2 + 1/2 gy^2 - Yt, quad 16 pi^2 ep thin (delta M^2_(Z gamma)) / M_Z^2 = - s_W c_W (35/12 gw^2 + 43/36 gy^2), \
  & 16 pi^2 ep thin (delta M_Z^2) / M_Z^2 = 3/2 gw^2 + 1/2 gy^2 - Yt - 35/6 gw^2 c_W^2 + 43/18 gy^2 s_W^2 . $
There is no $Ag dot Ag$ term.

_Gauge--Goldstone mixing._ The coefficients of the three structures of @eq:bl-L2mix are multiplied by $delta Z_H + delta Z_gw + delta Z_W \/ 2$, $delta Z_H + c_W^2 (delta Z_gw + delta Z_W\/2)$ and, for the new $Ag$--$G^0$ structure, $s_W c_W (delta Z_gw + delta Z_W\/2)$, with $delta Z_gw + delta Z_W \/ 2 = -C^((W))_"ad" lfe = -2 gw^2 lfe$ and $delta Z_gy + delta Z_B \/ 2 = 0$:
$ delta cal(L)^((1)) supset lfe [ & i M_W (2 C_H - Yt - 2 gw^2)(W^- dot partial G^+ - W^+ dot partial G^-) \
  & + M_Z (2 C_H - Yt - 2 gw^2 c_W^2) Z dot partial G^0 - 2 gw^2 s_W c_W M_Z thin Ag dot partial G^0 ] . $ <eq:bl-dS-mix>

_Scalar sector._ With $Phi_2$ of @eq:bl-Lint,
#eqbox[$ delta cal(L)^((1)) supset & delta Z_H [partial G^+ dot partial G^- + 1/2 (partial G^0)^2 + 1/2 (partial h)^2] - v thin delta T thin h - 1/2 (M_h^2 delta Z_H + delta M_h^2 + delta T) h^2 \
  & - delta T (G^+ G^- + 1/2 (G^0)^2) - (delta lambda + 2 lambda delta Z_H) (v h Phi_2 + 1/4 Phi_2^2) , $ <eq:bl-dS-scalar>]
$ & delta T = delta m^2 + v^2 delta lambda + lambda v^2 delta Z_H = lfe thin v^2 (6 lambda^2 - lambda C_H - Y_4 + 3/16 G_4), \
  & delta M_h^2 = M_h^2 ((delta lambda) / lambda + delta Z_H) , $ <eq:bl-dT>
with
$ & 16 pi^2 ep thin ((delta lambda) / lambda + delta Z_H) = 12 lambda - 4 C_H + Yt + (3/16 G_4 - Y_4) / lambda , \
  & 16 pi^2 ep thin (delta lambda + 2 lambda delta Z_H) = 12 lambda^2 - 2 lambda C_H - Y_4 + 3/16 G_4 . $
The term $-v thin delta T thin h$ is the tadpole counterterm; it cancels the pole of the one-loop tadpole. Its $lambda^2$ part is the pole $6 lambda^2 v^3 lfe$ of the $h$ loop (checked by hand); the other parts of the tadpole were not recomputed. The Goldstone mass counterterm equals $delta T$, as required by $Gamma_(G G)(0) = Gamma_h \/ v$ once tadpoles are included ($Gamma_h$ is the one-point function of $h$). $delta T$ contains the field-renormalisation part $lambda v^2 delta Z_H$ besides $delta m^2 + v^2 delta lambda$.

_Fermions._ With $delta Z_(u_upright(L)) = delta Z_(d_upright(L)) = delta Z_Q$, $delta Z_(nu_upright(L)) = delta Z_(e_upright(L)) = delta Z_L$, $delta Z_(u_upright(R)) = delta Z_U$, $delta Z_(d_upright(R)) = delta Z_D$, $delta Z_(e_upright(R)) = delta Z_E$:
$ delta cal(L)^((1)) supset sum_f overline(f) i slb(partial) (delta Z_(f_upright(L)) PL + delta Z_(f_upright(R)) PR) f + sum_(k = u, d, e) c_k cal(L)_("Yuk", k) + sum_(f, r) delta^(f r)_V overline(Psi)_f gbar^mu Am^((r))_mu P_(c_f) Psi_f , $ <eq:bl-dS-ferm>
where $cal(L)_("Yuk", k)$ is the part of @eq:bl-yuk proportional to $m_k$ (mass term, $h$, $G^0$ and $G^plus.minus$ couplings alike), $c_k = (delta y_k)\/y_k + (delta Z_H + delta Z_(k_upright(L)) + delta Z_(k_upright(R)))\/2$, and $delta^(f r)_V = delta Z_f + delta Z_(c_r) + delta Z^((r))_A \/ 2 = -(C_f + C^((r))_"ad" + cal(Y)_f) lfe$ multiplies the current of factor $r$ (in the mass basis through @eq:bl-Am). In the Standard Model
$ & 16 pi^2 ep thin c_u = -(16/3 gs^2 + 3/4 gw^2 + 25/36 gy^2 + y_d^2), quad 16 pi^2 ep thin c_d = -(16/3 gs^2 + 3/4 gw^2 + 1/36 gy^2 + y_u^2), \
  & 16 pi^2 ep thin c_e = -(3/4 gw^2 + 9/4 gy^2) . $
Here $k = u, d, e$ labels the massive fermion $psi_k$, with $psi_u = u$, $psi_d = d$, $psi_e = e$ of @eq:bl-fermions. Its mass counterterm is $-m_k c_k overline(psi)_k psi_k = -(delta m_k + m_k (delta Z_(k_upright(L)) + delta Z_(k_upright(R)))\/2) overline(psi)_k psi_k$, with the bare-mass shift $delta m_k = m_k ((delta y_k) \/ y_k + delta Z_H \/ 2)$:
$ & 16 pi^2 ep thin (delta m_u)/m_u = 3/4 (y_u^2 - y_d^2) - 4 gs^2 - 3/8 gw^2 - 11/24 gy^2, quad 16 pi^2 ep thin (delta m_d)/m_d = 3/4 (y_d^2 - y_u^2) - 4 gs^2 - 3/8 gw^2 + 1/24 gy^2, \
  & 16 pi^2 ep thin (delta m_e)/m_e = 3/4 y_e^2 - 3/8 gw^2 - 13/8 gy^2 . $
The sterile kinetic terms and the evanescent terms $overline(f) i slh(partial) f' + overline(f)' i slh(partial) f$ are not renormalised.

_Ghosts and sources._ The ghost kinetic term receives $(tilde(Z)_3 - 1) partial agh^a dot partial gh^a$ with $tilde(Z)_3 - 1 = 1/2 C^((r))_"ad" lfe$, i.e.
$ lfe { & gw^2 [partial agh^+ dot partial gh^- + partial agh^- dot partial gh^+ + (c_W partial agh^Z + s_W partial agh^gamma) dot (c_W partial gh^Z + s_W partial gh^gamma)] \
  & + 3/2 gs^2 partial agh^A dot partial gh^A } . $
The ghost--gauge vertex and all non-linear source terms are multiplied by $tilde(Z)_1 - 1 = -1/2 C^((r))_"ad" lfe$. With $H = Hv + phi$ the latter contains $-gw^2 lfe [i srcH^dagger wm^((W)) Hv + "h.c."]$, with $wm^((W)) Hv = M_W (gh^+, -(c_W gh^Z + s_W gh^gamma)\/sqrt(2))^T$.

*(b) Structure in $d$ dimensions.* The graphs without a closed fermion loop give the closed directions continued with unsplit $d$-dimensional indices. The closed fermion loops give only barred invariants: $-2/3 S^((r)) lfe integral (-1/4 bar(F)^((r)) dot bar(F)^((r)))$, $-Yt lfe integral (bar(D) H)^dagger dot bar(D) H$ and $+Y_4 lfe thin Q_lambda$ (@eq:c-dS-ev and the text after it). At $H = Hv + phi$ the Yukawa (fermion-loop) part of every term built from $(D H)^dagger D H$ therefore carries barred components only. In @eq:bl-dS-mass the gauge-coupling parts ($-4 gw^2$, $-4 gw^2 c_W^2$, the $Z dot Ag$ term and $2 C_H$) come from bosonic loops and multiply the unsplit $W^+ dot W^- = bar(W)^+ dot bar(W)^- + hat(W)^+ dot hat(W)^-$, $Z dot Z$, $Z dot Ag$. The Yukawa part is
$ delta cal(L)^((1)) supset - Yt lfe [ & M_W^2 bar(W)^+ dot bar(W)^- + 1/2 M_Z^2 bar(Z) dot bar(Z) + M_Z bar(Z) dot bar(partial) G^0 \
  & + i M_W (bar(W)^- dot bar(partial) G^+ - bar(W)^+ dot bar(partial) G^-) + bar(partial) phi^dagger dot bar(partial) phi] , $ <eq:bl-dS-bar>
with barred components only; it has no $Z dot Ag$ and no $Ag dot Ag$ part. Likewise the fermion-loop parts of $16 pi^2 ep thin delta Z_W$ and $16 pi^2 ep thin delta Z_B$ ($-4/3 gw^2$, $-20/9 gy^2$) multiply barred kinetic terms; the bosonic parts are $19/6 gw^2$ and $-1/6 gy^2$ (and $5 gs^2$ against $-4/3 gs^2$ for gluons). In the form @eq:c-dS-ev the same content reads: unsplit terms everywhere plus $-Yt lfe thin tilde(E)_H [Hv + phi]$, whose mass part is $+Yt lfe (M_W^2 hat(W)^+ dot hat(W)^- + 1/2 M_Z^2 hat(Z) dot hat(Z))$.

*(c) Evanescent non-invariant terms.* $E_H$ does not see the constant $Hv$, and $E^((r))_A$ does not contain $H$:
$ & - 2/3 Yt lfe thin E_H [Hv + phi] = - 2/3 Yt lfe integral dif^d x [hat(partial) G^+ dot hat(partial) G^- + 1/2 (hat(partial) h)^2 + 1/2 (hat(partial) G^0)^2] , \
  & - 1/3 lfe sum_r S^((r)) E^((r))_A = - lfe integral dif^d x [ 2/3 gw^2 bar(W)^+ dot hat(partial)^2 bar(W)^- + 1/3 gs^2 bar(G)^A dot hat(partial)^2 bar(G)^A \
  & #h(12em) + 1/9 (3 gw^2 bar(W)^3 dot hat(partial)^2 bar(W)^3 + 5 gy^2 bar(B) dot hat(partial)^2 bar(B)) ] . $ <eq:bl-EA>
With @eq:bl-combo the neutral part of the last bracket is $(3 gw^2 c_W^2 + 5 gy^2 s_W^2)\/9 thin bar(Z) dot hat(partial)^2 bar(Z) + 2 e (3 gw c_W - 5 gy s_W)\/9 thin bar(Z) dot hat(partial)^2 bar(A)^gamma + 8/9 e^2 bar(A)^gamma dot hat(partial)^2 bar(A)^gamma$. The photon coefficient is $1/3 e^2 sum_f N^c_f q_f^2 = 8/9 e^2$.

=== The finite restoring counterterm <sec:bl-ST>

Every formula below gives $16 pi^2$ times a term of $Delta S^((1))_"ST" = lf sum_alpha r_alpha Q_alpha$, with the $r_alpha$ of @tab:sts-r (bars omitted: four-dimensional fields, indices and derivatives). Two independent solutions of the Slavnov--Taylor conditions agree in all 39 non-zero coefficients (@sec:st-solution). The $H$-dependent coefficients are $r^((W))_J = r^((B))_J = Yt\/3$, $r_(W W) = -Yt$, $r_(B B) = -(13/3 y_u^2 + 7/3 y_d^2 + 3 y_e^2)$, $r_(W B) = -(y_u^2 + 2 y_d^2)$, $r_(G G) = -1/2 (y_u^2 + y_d^2)$, $r^((r))_D = r^((W))_sigma = 0$ (@eq:bp-r1).

*(a) Bilinear terms.* _Longitudinal_ (from $Q^((r))_L$, $r_L = -2/3 gs^2, -2/3 gw^2, -10/9 gy^2$):
$ 16 pi^2 Delta cal(L)_L = 2/3 gw^2 (partial dot W^+)(partial dot W^-) + 1/9 [3 (gw thin partial dot W^3)^2 + 5 (gy thin partial dot B)^2] + 1/3 gs^2 (partial dot G^A)^2 , $ <eq:bl-L>
i.e. with @eq:bl-combo $(3 gw^2 c_W^2 + 5 gy^2 s_W^2)\/9 thin (partial dot Z)^2 + 2 e (3 gw c_W - 5 gy s_W)\/9 thin (partial dot Z)(partial dot Ag) + 8/9 e^2 (partial dot Ag)^2$. The photon and gluon coefficients are $1/3 e^2 sum_f N^c_f q_f^2$ and $1/3 gs^2 sum_q T_F$ ($T_F = 1/2$, two quarks).

_Mass-like_ (from $Q_(W W)$, $Q_(B B)$, $Q_(W B)$, $Q_(G G)$ at $H = Hv$):
$ 16 pi^2 Delta cal(L)_M = & r_(W W) M_W^2 W^+ dot W^- + v^2/8 [r_(W W) (gw W^3)^2 + r_(B B) (gy B)^2 - 2 r_(W B) (gw W^3) dot (gy B)] \
  & + 1/2 r_(G G) gs^2 v^2 G^A dot G^A , $ <eq:bl-M-def>
#eqbox[$ 16 pi^2 Delta cal(L)_M = & - gw^2/2 (3 m_u^2 + 3 m_d^2 + m_e^2) W^+ dot W^- - 1/2 gs^2 (m_u^2 + m_d^2) G^A dot G^A \
  & + 1/2 sum_(V, V' in {Z, gamma}) Delta M^2_(V V') A^V dot A^(V') . $ <eq:bl-M>]
$V, V'$ label the neutral gauge bosons ($A^Z = Z$, $A^gamma = Ag$). The coefficients $Delta M^2_(V V')$ are, like the $r_alpha$, free of the factor $lf$:
$ & Delta M^2_(V V') = -2 sum_(f = u, d, e) N^c_f m_f^2 (v^V_f v^(V')_f + 3 a^V_f a^(V')_f), \
  & v^gamma_f = e q_f, quad a^gamma_f = 0, quad v^Z_f = gw/(2 c_W) (T^3_f - 2 s_W^2 q_f), quad a^Z_f = gw/(2 c_W) T^3_f , $ <eq:bl-dMVV>
with the vector and axial couplings $v^V_f$, $a^V_f$ of $f$ to $V$. Explicitly,
$ & Delta M^2_(gamma gamma) = -2 e^2 sum_f N^c_f q_f^2 m_f^2 = -2 e^2 (4/3 m_u^2 + 1/3 m_d^2 + m_e^2), quad Delta M^2_(Z gamma) = -e gw/c_W sum_f N^c_f q_f (T^3_f - 2 s_W^2 q_f) m_f^2, \
  & Delta M^2_(Z Z) = -(gw^2)/(c_W^2) sum_f N^c_f m_f^2 [3/2 (T^3_f)^2 + 1/2 (T^3_f - 2 s_W^2 q_f)^2] . $
The $W$ term has the same form with $v^W = a^W = gw\/(2 sqrt(2))$ and the average $(m_"up"^2 + m_"down"^2)\/2$ of each doublet. The photon term is proportional to $e^2 sum_f N^c_f q_f^2 m_f^2$ and the gluon term to $gs^2 sum_q m_q^2$; @sec:bl-massless shows that they cancel the finite mass terms of the fermion loops. Both were verified from $r_(W W)$, $r_(B B)$, $r_(W B)$, $r_(G G)$, and they agree with @eq:bp-dM-1loop.

_Gauge--Goldstone and gauge--$h$ mixing_ (from $Q^((r))_J$, $Q^((r))_D$):
$ 16 pi^2 Delta cal(L)_"mix" = - Yt/3 [M_Z Z dot partial G^0 + i M_W (W^- dot partial G^+ - W^+ dot partial G^-)] = - Yt/3 cal(L)^(V G)_2 , $ <eq:bl-mix>
with $Yt$ of @eq:bl-sums.
There is no $Ag$--$G^0$ term ($r^((W))_J = r^((B))_J$) and no gauge--$h$ term ($r^((r))_D = 0$).

*(b) Terms with $phi$.* Every $phi$-dependence of $Q_(W W)$, $Q_(B B)$, $Q_(W B)$, $Q_(G G)$ is
#eqbox[$ 16 pi^2 Delta cal(L)_(M, phi) = & ((1 + h/v)^2 - 1) 16 pi^2 Delta cal(L)_M \
  & + (G^+ G^- + 1/2 (G^0)^2) [r_(W W) gw^2/4 W^I dot W^I + r_(B B)/4 (gy B)^2 + r_(G G) gs^2 G^A dot G^A] \
  & + r_(W B)/2 (gy B) dot [gw (v + h)(W^+ G^- + W^- G^+) + i gw G^0 (W^+ G^- - W^- G^+) \
  & #h(5.5em) + gw W^3 (G^+ G^- - 1/2 (G^0)^2)] , $ <eq:bl-Mphi>]
with $W^I dot W^I = 2 W^+ dot W^- + W^3 dot W^3$ and @eq:bl-combo. The $h$-linear terms are $2 h\/v$ times @eq:bl-M; the only other term linear in $phi$ is $r_(W B) M_W (e Ag - gy s_W Z) dot (G^+ W^- + G^- W^+) = -(y_u^2 + 2 y_d^2) M_W (e Ag - gy s_W Z) dot (G^+ W^- + G^- W^+)$. With the values of $r_alpha$, $(1 + h\/v)^2$ multiplies the fermion-mass form @eq:bl-M. The $phi$-dependence of $Q^((r))_J$ is
$ 16 pi^2 Delta cal(L)_(J) = Yt/3 thin i [(partial_mu phi)^dagger Am^mu (Hv + phi) - (Hv + phi)^dagger Am^mu partial_mu phi] , $ <eq:bl-J>
with $Am = Am^((W)) + Am^((B))$ of @eq:bl-Am on the doublet.
Its $phi$-linear part is @eq:bl-mix and its $phi phi V$ part is $-Yt\/3$ times the corresponding tree vertex, since $Q^((W))_J + Q^((B))_J = -[(D H)^dagger D H]_(A "-linear")$. $Q^((r))_D$ and $Q^((W))_sigma$ vanish: no $h$--gauge term, and no change of @eq:bl-sphi.

*(c) Terms the shift does not touch.* The remaining 33 non-zero coefficients of @tab:sts-r multiply monomials without $H$: 3 of $Q^((r))_L$, 2 of $Q^((r))_(3 f)$, 13 quartic gauge monomials, 10 of $Q^(f r)_V$ and 5 of $Q^(f r)_R$. They are the gauge-field, fermion--gauge and source parts of @eq:c-DS (@sec:st-solution) and read, in gauge eigenstates,
$ 16 pi^2 Delta cal(L)_"rest" = & 2/3 gs^3 f^(A B C) (partial_mu G^A_nu) G^(B mu) G^(C nu) + 2/3 gw^3 epsilon^(I J K) (partial_mu W^I_nu) W^(J mu) W^(K nu) \
  & + gs^4 [11/72 (G dot G)^2 - 1/4 (G^A dot G^B)^2 + 5/12 d^(A B E) d^(C D E) (G^A dot G^B)(G^C dot G^D)] \
  & + gw^4 [7/24 (W^I dot W^I)^2 - 1/4 (W^I dot W^J)^2] + 95/648 gy^4 (B dot B)^2 \
  & + 1/18 gs^3 gy d^(A C D) (G^A dot G^C)(G^D dot B) \
  & + sum_(r s) k_(r s) c_r^2 c_s^2 [1/2 (A_((r)) dot A_((r)))(A_((s)) dot A_((s))) + (A^a_((r)) dot A^b_((s)))^2] \
  & - sum_f overline(psi)_f gamma^mu [C_f Am_mu + 1/2 sum_(r in f) nu_(f r) Am^((r))_mu] psi_f - 1/4 sum_f [i overline(srcF)_f wm_C psi_f - i overline(psi)_f wm_C srcF_f] , $ <eq:bl-rest>
with $k_(G W) = 1/12$, $k_(G B) = 11/108$, $k_(W B) = 1/18$ (sum over the pairs $r s = G W, G B, W B$). The last line is the second line of @eq:c-DS, with $nu_(f r)$ of @sec:Sren1 and $wm_C = 3 gs^2 wm^((G)) + 2 gw^2 wm^((W))$, i.e. $r[Q^(f G)_R] = -3/4 gs^2$, $r[Q^(f W)_R] = -1/2 gw^2$. The rotation to the mass basis: $W^(1,2) -> W^plus.minus$ and $W^3$, $B$ by @eq:bl-combo; for three adjoint vectors $epsilon^(I J K) X^I Y^J U^K = i [U^3 (X^- Y^+ - X^+ Y^-) + "cyclic"]$; the same for ghosts in $wm^((W))$; the quartic terms are left in this form. In the fermion terms @eq:bl-Am gives: $-C_f overline(psi)_f gamma^mu Am_mu psi_f$ is $-C_f$ times the tree current of the multiplet $f$, whose mass-basis form follows @eq:bl-Lint, and
$ - 1/2 sum_(f, r) nu_(f r) overline(psi)_f gamma^mu Am^((r))_mu psi_f = & - gs G^A dot [(y_u^2 + y_d^2)/2 overline(psi)_Q gamma T^A psi_Q + y_u^2 overline(u)_upright(R) gamma T^A u_upright(R) + y_d^2 overline(d)_upright(R) gamma T^A d_upright(R)] \
  & - (e Ag - gy s_W Z) dot [(2 y_u^2 - y_d^2)/6 overline(psi)_Q gamma psi_Q + y_u^2/6 overline(u)_upright(R) gamma u_upright(R) + y_d^2/6 overline(d)_upright(R) gamma d_upright(R) \
  & #h(8em) - y_e^2/2 (overline(psi)_L gamma psi_L + overline(e)_upright(R) gamma e_upright(R))] , $ <eq:bl-nu>
with the physical doublets $psi_Q = (u_upright(L), d_upright(L))$, $psi_L = (nu_upright(L), e_upright(L))$, e.g. $overline(psi)_Q gamma psi_Q = overline(u)_upright(L) gamma u_upright(L) + overline(d)_upright(L) gamma d_upright(L)$. The Yukawa parts couple only through $gy B$ and the gluon; they are not proportional to $q_f$.

